=base:summary.cmark

A `corporate` layout example: a fictional marketing page for an "Acme
Cloud" product, composed from the `corporate.cmark-tramaj` component
library (hero, feature grid, pricing table, call to action, testimonial
strip) instead of hand-written HTML.

=base:dataset.json hero-data
{ "title": "Acme Cloud"
, "subtitle": "Track team spend in real time, without the spreadsheet gymnastics. Set up in an afternoon, keep everyone honest for years."
, "actions":
  [ {"label": "See pricing", "href": "#pricing", "style": "primary"}
  , {"label": "Talk to sales", "href": "#contact", "style": "secondary"}
  ]
}

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@d=$ctx.datasets.hero-data
import("corporate/hero", {"title": $d.title, "subtitle": $d.subtitle, "actions": $d.actions}).rendered

=base:dataset.json features-data
{ "features":
  [ {"title": "Live budgets", "body": "Every team sees its own bucket update as spend happens, not at month-end reconciliation."}
  , {"title": "Delegated keys", "body": "Hand a scoped key to a sub-team or a robot; reclaim what it does not use."}
  , {"title": "Audit trail", "body": "Every consumption and replenishment is timestamped and attributable, no export required."}
  ]
}

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@d=$ctx.datasets.features-data
.(.h2("Why teams switch to Acme Cloud"),
  import("corporate/feature-grid", {"features": $d.features}).rendered)

=base:dataset.json pricing-data
{ "plans":
  [ {"name": "Starter", "price": "$0"}
  , {"name": "Team", "price": "$29/mo"}
  , {"name": "Scale", "price": "Talk to us"}
  ]
, "rows":
  [ {"feature": "Buckets", "values": ["3", "25", "Unlimited"]}
  , {"feature": "Delegated keys", "values": ["1", "20", "Unlimited"]}
  , {"feature": "Support", "values": ["Community", "Priority", "Dedicated"]}
  ]
}

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@d=$ctx.datasets.pricing-data
import("corporate/pricing-table", {"plans": $d.plans, "rows": $d.rows}).rendered

=base:dataset.json testimonials-data
{ "testimonials":
  [ {"quote": "We went from a shared spreadsheet nobody trusted to a dashboard every team lead checks before standup.", "author": "Head of Platform, mid-size fintech"}
  , {"quote": "Delegated keys are the feature that sold the rest of the team: our robots finally have their own budget instead of one shared secret.", "author": "Staff engineer, dev tooling team"}
  ]
}

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@d=$ctx.datasets.testimonials-data
.(.h2("What our early customers say"),
  import("corporate/testimonial-strip", {"testimonials": $d.testimonials}).rendered)

=base:dataset.json cta-data
{ "title": "Ready to see it on your own numbers?"
, "body": "No credit card. Import a CSV of last month's spend and get a live dashboard in minutes."
, "label": "Get started"
, "href": "mailto:hello@example.invalid"
, "id": "contact"
}

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@d=$ctx.datasets.cta-data
import("corporate/cta-banner", {"title": $d.title, "body": $d.body, "label": $d.label, "href": $d.href, "id": $d.id}).rendered

=base:main-content.cmark

<p>&#8203;</p>

This page uses the <code>corporate</code> article layout: set
<code>{"layout":"corporate"}</code> in <code>base:build-info.json</code> and
import <code>/css/corporate.css</code> next to the usual stylesheets. Unlike
the <code>article</code> layout, it renders no byline, no publication date,
and no topic links or glossary — only the site-wide menu and footer plus
whatever sections the page declares, each as its own full-width section.
Every section above is a `main-content.tramaj-doc` section that reads a
`dataset.json` cell and imports a component from
[`corporate.cmark-tramaj`](/corporate-components.html), rather than
hand-written HTML per page. See [layouts](/layouts.html) for the other
article layouts and [corporate components](/corporate-components.html) for
the library's documented fields.
